2026-04-05 09:11:37.159 | 24908 (24908) | DEBUG    | Model request part: {"tool_name": "open_files", "content": ["Successfully opened memory-bank/projectbrief.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Project Brief - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 ## Vision\n   3 To create the most comprehensive AI-powered writing and document generation platform that empowers academics, professionals, and students to produce high-quality, context-aware content efficiently and effectively.\n   4 \n   5 ## Mission\n   6 Arkan serves as an intelligent writing assistant that combines cutting-edge AI technology with a dynamic, retrieval-augmented knowledge base to democratize access to professional-grade writing and document creation tools.\n   7 \n   8 ## Project Goals\n   9 \n  10 ### Primary Goals\n  11 - **Comprehensive Writing Support**: Provide 23+ AI-powered writing tools.\n  12 - **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)**: Enhance AI responses with grounded context from a vector database.\n  13 - **Professional Document Generation**: Support high-fidelity report, proposal, and presentation synthesis.\n  14 - **Multi-language Support**: Full Arabic and English support with native RTL capabilities.\n  15 - **Production Resilience**: Maintain 100% type safety and architectural robustness under Next.js 15.\n  16 \n  17 ## Core Features\n  18 \n  19 ### AI Writing Tools (23+ Tools)\n  20 - Content Generation, Manipulation, and Quality Assurance.\n  21 \n  22 ### Advanced Capabilities\n  23 - **RAG System**: Qdrant-powered semantic search and context retrieval.\n  24 - **Manifest Document Engine**: Multi-node document synthesis with DOCX/PPTX export.\n  25 - **Spectral Analysis**: Deep decomposition of source matrices into structural intelligence.\n  26 \n  27 ### Platform Features\n  28 - **Admin Dashboard**: System-wide oversight, user management, and broadcast protocols.\n  29 - **Identity & Billing**: Secure authentication with hardware fingerprinting and credit-based acquisition.\n  30 \n  31 ## Success Metrics\n  32 - MAU, guest-to-user conversion, RAG relevance scores, and document synthesis volume.\n  33 \n  34 ## Technology Foundation\n  35 - **Next.js 15 / React 19**, TypeScript, Google Genkit, Qdrant, SQLite (Drizzle), Tailwind CSS.\n  36 \n  37 ## Current Status\n  38 Arkan is a **production-hardened**, high-performance application. Following a massive robustness refactor in April 2026, the project has reached 100% Clean Architecture compliance and zero-tolerance type safety. The current focus is on performance scaling, RAG retrieval optimization, and expanding test coverage.\n  39 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/productContext.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Product Context - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 ## Product Vision\n   3 Arkan is the most comprehensive AI-powered writing and document generation platform, designed to empower academics, professionals, and students to create high-quality content efficiently and effectively.\n   4 \n   5 ## Product Mission\n   6 To democratize access to professional-grade writing tools by leveraging cutting-edge AI technology, making advanced content creation capabilities accessible to users regardless of their technical expertise or geographical location.\n   7 \n   8 ## Target Market & Audience\n   9 \n  10 ### Primary Segments\n  11 - **Academic Researchers & Students**: Focus on citation stability, structural logic, and research synthesis.\n  12 - **Business Professionals**: Focus on report production, executive summaries, and presentation synthesis.\n  13 - **Educational Institutions**: Focus on lecture generation and assignment solving.\n  14 \n  15 ### Geographic Markets\n  16 - **Primary**: Middle East & North Africa (MENA) with native Arabic/RTL support.\n  17 - **Secondary**: International English-speaking markets.\n  18 \n  19 ## Core Product Features\n  20 \n  21 ### AI Writing Tools Suite (23+ Tools)\n  22 - Flagship tools: Summarizer, Researcher, Stylist, and Document Writer.\n  23 \n  24 ### Document Generation System\n  25 - **Report Mode**: Multi-node, template-driven synthesis with high-fidelity DOCX export.\n  26 - **Presentation Builder**: AI slide generation with PPTX production manifest.\n  27 - **Spectral Analysis**: Deep decomposition of source data into manageable structural intelligence.\n  28 \n  29 ### Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\n  30 - **Context-Aware Generation**: Grounded AI responses using the centralized Knowledge Base.\n  31 - **Admin Oversight**: Document indexer, query tester, and system health monitoring.\n  32 \n  33 ## Product Differentiation\n  34 \n  35 ### Unique Value Propositions\n  36 1. **Intelligence Suite Aesthetic**: A professional, technical \"IDE-style\" interaction model.\n  37 2. **Production Robustness**: Zero-tolerance for runtime errors via defensive programming and neural error boundaries.\n  38 3. **Cultural Adaptation**: Native support for Arabic and RTL layouts.\n  39 4. **State Integrity**: Atomic synchronization of document manifests across multi-step processes.\n  40 \n  41 ### Competitive Advantages\n  42 \n  43 #### Technology Stack\n  44 - **Next.js 15 / React 19**: Utilizing the latest concurrent features and server-side optimizations.\n  45 - **Qdrant Vector Store**: Sub-100ms search latency for high-scale context retrieval.\n  46 - **Resilient AI Flows**: Tiered fallback logic and structured Result vectors.\n  47 \n  48 #### User Experience\n  49 - **IDE Pattern**: 3-zone workspace optimized for complex document production.\n  50 - **Manifest Interaction Model**: Technical, multi-step manifests for critical operations (Build, Export, Acquisition).\n  51 - **Stable Manifests**: Operational feedback via pulsing status nodes and versioned manifest footers.\n  52 \n  53 ## Business Model\n  54 - **Primary**: Credit-based acquisition for advanced AI operations.\n  55 - **Secondary**: Subscription tiers for institutional access.\n  56 \n  57 ## Success Metrics & KPIs\n  58 - MAU, retention, credit acquisition volume, and RAG relevance scores.\n  59 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/systemPatterns.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # System Patterns - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 ## Architectural Patterns\n   3 \n   4 ### 1. Strict Clean Architecture (DDD)\n   5 **Purpose**: Absolute separation of concerns between business logic, orchestration, and infrastructure.\n   6 - **Implementation**: 4-layer structure in `src/modules/` (`domain`, `application`, `adapters`, `infrastructure`).\n   7 \n   8 ### 2. Modular AI & Schema Pattern\n   9 **Purpose**: Standardized approach for AI operations with unified data contracts.\n  10 - **Standard**: All AI flows return structured `Result<T, E>` objects.\n  11 - **Spectral Sanitization**: Mandatory use of `cleanAiOutput` to strip model conversational artifacts.\n  12 \n  13 ### 3. Client-Server DI Bridging Pattern\n  14 **Purpose**: Enabling high-weight services (e.g., Document Export) to be invoked from the client while executing on the server.\n  15 - **Implementation**: Lightweight `ExportApiClient` proxies registered for browser environments that delegate to server API routes, while full infrastructure services remain isolated on the server.\n  16 \n  17 ### 4. Standardized Domain Property Pattern\n  18 **Purpose**: Enforcing type safety and predictable state management for domain entities.\n  19 - **Pattern**: Entities utilize `toProperties()`, `toStateObject()`, and `withProps()`.\n  20 \n  21 ## State Management Patterns\n  22 \n  23 ### 1. Zustand Store Pattern (Client-side)\n  24 **Purpose**: Lightweight global state management for UI and session data.\n  25 - **Usage**: Manages active projects and application status. Uses atomic selectors to minimize re-renders.\n  26 \n  27 ### 2. Atomic State Transformation Pattern\n  28 **Purpose**: Preventing race conditions and ensuring state consistency during multi-node updates.\n  29 - **Implementation**: Using functional reduction (e.g., `targets.reduce((p, id) => p.updateSection(id, ...), project)`) within a single `updateProject` callback.\n  30 \n  31 ### 3. React Query Pattern (Server-side Cache)\n  32 **Purpose**: Server state management with caching and optimistic updates.\n  33 \n  34 ## Robustness & Resilience Patterns\n  35 \n  36 ### 1. Unified Existence Guard Pattern\n  37 **Purpose**: Preventing runtime crashes on partially hydrated or null state.\n  38 - **Implementation**: Explicit `if (!project || !userProfile) return` patterns in all interaction handlers.\n  39 \n  40 ### 2. Neural Error Boundary Pattern\n  41 **Purpose**: Containing rendering failures within specific UI zones to prevent full-page crashes.\n  42 - **Implementation**: `RendererErrorBoundary` wrapped around the document canvas and analysis hubs.\n  43 \n  44 ### 3. Selection Recovery Pattern\n  45 **Purpose**: Synchronizing structural shifts with UI interaction states.\n  46 - **Implementation**: \"Selection Recovery\" sweeps that automatically clear or update active focuses when nodes are deleted.\n  47 \n  48 ### 4. Persistence Containment Pattern\n  49 **Purpose**: Ensuring unhandled errors in async pipelines don't compromise session stability.\n  50 - **Implementation**: Mandatory `try-catch` blocks around all project mutations, external service calls, and AST transformations.\n  51 \n  52 ## UI/UX & Architecture Patterns\n  53 \n  54 ### 1. 3-Zone Workspace Architecture (IDE Pattern)\n  55 **Purpose**: Maximizing focus for complex document production.\n  56 \n  57 ### 2. Manifest Interaction Model\n  58 **Purpose**: Professional technical manifests for multi-step operations (Build, Export, Acquisition).\n  59 - **Aesthetic**: 28px dot-grids, glassmorphism, and active status pulses.\n  60 \n  61 ### 3. Stable Manifest Footer\n  62 **Purpose**: Providing version context and operational status to the user.\n  63 - **Pattern**: Standardized footers (`v2.4.0-STABLE`) across all HUD panels.\n  64 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/techContext.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Technical Context - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 ## Technology Stack\n   3 \n   4 ### Frontend Framework\n   5 - **Next.js 15**: React-based full-stack framework.\n   6 - **React 19**: Standardized top-level hook placement for stable concurrent rendering.\n   7 - **TypeScript**: Strict-mode type safety with mandatory `unknown` narrowing.\n   8 \n   9 ### AI Integration\n  10 - **Google Genkit**: Core AI orchestration framework.\n  11 - **Result Pattern**: Uniform `Result<T, E>` return vectors for all flows.\n  12 - **Clean AI Output**: Global utility for stripping model artifacts and markdown artifacts.\n  13 - **Tiered Fallback**: Automated model degradation (Llama -> Phi -> Gemma) for 8GB stability.\n  14 \n  15 ### Backend Services\n  16 - **Database**: SQLite with Drizzle ORM.\n  17 - **Vector Database**: Qdrant (`arkan_vectors` collection, 768 dims).\n  18 - **File Storage**: Local filesystem (`storage/uploads`) with traversal protection.\n  19 \n  20 ### UI Framework\n  21 - **shadcn/ui**: Built on Radix UI and Tailwind CSS.\n  22 - **Intelligence Suite Aesthetic**: High-density typography, technical grids, and pulsing status nodes.\n  23 \n  24 ## Architecture Patterns\n  25 \n  26 ### Dependency Injection (DI)\n  27 - **tsyringe**: Registered in `container.ts`.\n  28 - **\"use server\" Constraints**: Strict isolation of infrastructure classes from server action directives to prevent Next.js 15 class-export errors.\n  29 - **Bridging Pattern**: API Client proxies for browser-side DI resolution.\n  30 \n  31 ### RAG Architecture\n  32 - **Indexing & Retrieval**: Multi-layer LRU cache for embeddings and search results.\n  33 \n  34 ### Security Architecture\n  35 - **Auth Node**: Local JWT-based sessions with Bcrypt hashing and Jose token management.\n  36 - **Hardware Fingerprinting**: Async hardware profiling during identity creation.\n  37 - **Guard Node**: Robust optimistic rollback for security parameter synchronization.\n  38 \n  39 ## Performance Optimization\n  40 - **Atomic State Transformations**: Single-pass store mutations to prevent virtual DOM overhead.\n  41 - **Component Memoization**: Extensive use of `React.memo` for workspace components.\n  42 - **Code Splitting**: Automatic per-route splitting with Next.js Image optimization.\n  43 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/activeContext.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Active Context - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 ## Recently Completed\n   3 - **Clean Architecture Overhaul**: The project has reached a \"Gold Standard\" architectural state. All domain logic, state (Zustand), hooks, and smart components have been relocated into a self-contained module hierarchy (`src/modules/*`).\n   4 - **Robustness Refactoring & Global Hardening**: Completed a massive hardening pass across 50+ components (AI Builder, Admin, Profile, Billing). Implemented universal existence guards (`if (!project) return`), persistence containment (`try-catch`), and atomic state transformations.\n   5 - **Next.js 15 / React 19 Compliance**: Resolved critical \"Rules of Hooks\" violations by standardizing hook placement above early returns in all HUD components. Verified server action integrity.\n   6 - **Neural Flow Refinement**: Migrated all AI infrastructure flows to return structured `Result<T, E>` objects. Integrated `cleanAiOutput` as a mandatory post-processing step to ensure markdown purity.\n   7 - **Cross-Environment DI Bridging**: Established a pattern for services like **Document Export** that must be resolved on both client and server. Registered `ExportApiClient` proxies for the browser while maintaining full infrastructure implementations for the server.\n   8 - **Identity Consistency**: Standardized the `randomId()` utility project-wide, replacing unsafe `uuidv4` and timestamp-based identifiers across all document, source, and identity nodes.\n   9 - **Structural Integrity & Recovery**: Implemented automated \"Selection Recovery\" sweeps to clear orphaned UI states during structural deletions.\n  10 - **Neural Rendering Safety**: Introduced a dedicated `RendererErrorBoundary` for the document canvas and reinforced snapshot validation for the version comparison engine.\n  11 - **DI for React**: Standardized `useService(token)` pattern for resolving dependencies within the React lifecycle.\n  12 - **Platform-Wide Aesthetic Unification**: Finalized the \"Intelligence Suite\" visual standard across all HUDs, incorporating 28px dot-grids, high-density technical labels, and \"Stable Manifest\" footers with version indices.\n  13 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/recentUpdates.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Recent Updates - Arkan Memory Bank\n   1 \n   2 *Last Updated: April 2026*\n   3 \n   4 ## April 2026 Updates\n   5 \n   6 ### **Global Robustness Refactoring & Stability Hardening**\n   7 **Date**: April 2026\n   8 **Summary**: Completed an application-wide hardening pass across 50+ core components and infrastructure flows to ensure production-grade stability and Next.js 15 / React 19 compliance.\n   9 \n  10 - **Next.js 15 hook Integrity**: Audited all HUD components and resolved \"Rules of Hooks\" violations by standardizing top-level hook placement.\n  11 - **Atomic State Transformations**: Transitioned complex multi-node operations (Context Mapping, Structural Reordering, Settings Updates) to single-pass atomic reductions, eliminating state race conditions.\n  12 - **Defensive Programming Standards**: Codified universal existence guards (`if (!project) return`) and persistence containment (`try-catch`) across all UI interaction vectors.\n  13 - **Neural Flow Robustness**: Migrated core AI flows to the structured `Result<T, E>` return pattern and integrated mandatory `cleanAiOutput` sanitization for markdown purity.\n  14 - **Cross-Environment DI Bridging**: Resolved resolution errors by implementing API client proxies for client-side dependency injection, enabling DOCX and PPTX synthesis from the browser.\n  15 - **Identity & Structural Safety**: Standardized the project on `randomId()` for consistent node identification. Implemented \"Selection Recovery\" sweeps to clear orphaned focuses after structural deletions.\n  16 - **Neural Rendering Safety**: Introduced localized `RendererErrorBoundary` components and reinforced data validation for historical document snapshots.\n  17 - **Visual Aesthetic Unification**: Standardized the \"Intelligence Suite\" technical design across Generation, Source, Outline, Billing, Profile, and Admin modules.\n  18 \n  19 ## March 2026 Updates\n  20 \n  21 ### **AI Resilience & Domain Hardening**\n  22 - **Tiered Fallback Logic**: Implemented automated model degradation (Llama 3 \u2192 Phi-3 \u2192 Gemma 2B) to ensure 8GB RAM stability.\n  23 - **Standardized Entity Pattern**: Unified all domain entities on the `toProperties()` and `withProps()` pattern.\n  24 - **Client-Server SDK Decoupling**: Resolved critical bundling errors by isolating heavy server-side AI SDKs from the browser chunking context.\n  25 \n  26 ### **Clean Architecture Hardening & Firebase Decommissioning**\n  27 - **Clean Architecture Implementation**: Reached 100% DDD compliance across all modules.\n  28 - **Auth & Storage Localized**: Completed removal of Firebase Client SDKs. Implemented local SQLite auth and filesystem storage.\n  29 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/progress.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Progress Report - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 *Last Updated: April 2026*\n   3 \n   4 ## Development Milestones\n   5 \n   6 ### Phase 7: Production Stability & Robustness (Completed - April 2026)\n   7 \u2705 **Global Robustness Refactoring**: Hardened 50+ orchestration HUDs and components with defensive programming.\n   8 \u2705 **Next.js 15 / React 19 Compliance**: Standardized hook placement and resolved class-export directive conflicts.\n   9 \u2705 **Atomic State Hardening**: Implemented single-pass transformations for multi-node operations.\n  10 \u2705 **Neural Flow Resilience**: Transitioned AI flows to